    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39210" root="نبذ" body-key="n">
    
      8 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">انتبذ</span></b>  (tropical:)  <i>He went, withdrew,</i> or <i>retired,
aside,</i> or <i>apart,</i> from others; <i>separated himself from others.</i> (S, A, L, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">انتبذت</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَكَانًا</span> (Kur, xix. 16,) (tropical:)  <i>She withdrew,</i> or <i>retired,
to a place apart from her family,</i> (L, Msb,) <i>far
away.</i> (Msb.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِنْتَبَذَ عَنْ قَوْمِهِ</span> <i>He withdrew,</i>
or <i>retired, from his people.</i> (M.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِنتبذ نَاحِيَةً</span>
<i>He went aside.</i> (T.) See 1. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b5-  And see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِنْتَبَثَ</span>
in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نبث</span>.

